# Model Orchestration (Cursor Pro + Claude + Codex)

Use the right model for the job. Max Mode when context or reasoning depth matters.

## Default Model Map

| Task Type | Preferred Model | Mode |
|-----------|-----------------|------|
| Agent coding, refactors, PRs | GPT-5.3 Codex High / Composer 2.5 | Max for large repos |
| Deep architecture, specs, trade-offs | Claude 4.6/4.7 Opus or Sonnet | Max Mode |
| Long documents, resume/JD analysis | Claude Sonnet 5 or Opus | Max Mode |
| Fast edits, small fixes | Auto or GPT-5.4 Mini | Default |
| UI/visual from Figma | Claude Sonnet + Figma MCP | — |
| Cloud Agents (async) | Same as task; enable in dashboard | — |

## Cursor Pro Settings (User Action Required)

**Pro Mode / large context is the workspace default** (see `05-cursor-pro-mode.mdc` and `docs/CURSOR_PRO_MAX_MODE.md`).

### Turn it on in the IDE (agents cannot)

| Plan | Action |
|------|--------|
| Usage-based Pro | Agent model picker → **Edit** → **Context** = max (e.g. **1M**) |
| Legacy request | Model picker → **Max Mode** **ON** |

Also in **Cursor Settings → Models** (`Ctrl+Shift+J`):

1. Enable **Claude Opus/Sonnet**, **GPT-5.3 Codex**, **GPT-5.4** (Show hidden models if needed).
2. Default Agent Model: **Auto** daily; switch to Codex/Claude for heavy tasks.
3. Monitor usage at [cursor.com/settings](https://cursor.com/settings).

## Claude Pro (claude.ai) — When to Use Alongside Cursor

- Long research threads, artifact editing, Projects with uploaded docs.
- Resume/cover letter polish after Cursor draft.
- Paste Cursor output into Claude Projects for second-pass review.

## Codex / OpenAI — When to Use

- Heavy multi-file refactors and test-driven implementation in Cursor Agent.
- CLI and API design (use `cli-for-agents` skill patterns).
- Pair with Cursor Bugbot for PR review.

## Multi-Model Pipeline (Recommended)

```
JD/요구사항 → Cursor Agent (분석·초안) → Claude Pro (문장·전략 검토) → Cursor (최종 파일·PR)
코드 구현   → Codex/GPT-5.3 Codex (구현) → Claude Opus (아키텍처 리뷰) → CI/Bugbot
임베디드    → Claude Max (SM·타이밍·안전) → Codex (드라이버/펌웨어) → Cursor (측정·PR)
```

## Substantive Work Default

For multi-file, architecture, firmware, or long documents: load `cursor-pro-max-orchestration`, enable **Max Mode**, and route domain skills (`stm32-device-drivers`, `taeha-dispense-controller`, `resume-jd-match`, etc.) before coding.

Do not run duplicate paid calls for the same subtask unless quality requires a second pass.
